## **Part 5: Troubleshooting for VMware**

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| VMs can't ping each other | Verify all VMs are on `LabLAN` (LAN Segment). Restart network: `sudo netplan apply` |
| Dashboard not accessible from host | Verify SecBox has second NIC on `VMnet1` (Host-only) with IP `192.168.57.10`. Test: `ping 192.168.57.10` from host. |
| Detector doesn't see ARP packets | Verify detector is running on correct interface (`ip link show`). Use: `sudo tcpdump -i enp2s0 arp` to verify packets exist. |
| "arpspoof: command not found" | Install dsniff: `sudo apt install dsniff` on attacker VM. |
| Detector crashes with "Permission denied" | Always run with `sudo`: `sudo python3 arp_detector.py` |
| No alerts even after attack | Check detector log: `tail -f /tmp/arp_detector.log`. Verify attack is actually running on attacker. |

